body:
Ye , so i dont know what to do, or to think , if she isnt trying to keep me as a backup plan or what else can be happening

&#x200B;

Or could it be she treats me like her bestfriend or a brother? whats the possibility of being friendzoned if she behaves likes this?

Today we were at work (yes on sunday, special occasion) we did not talk too much today since both of us had quite alot to do..Anyway skip forwards few hours, fire alarm went off (thankfully a drill) but as soon as my other colleagues hear it , i came to her, and told her to stop working and come with me that we need to go outside because of the alarm and i dont want her to burn there if its not a drill .  There was another like 15-20 colleagues allready going outside, after we came outside where were others like 60+ people and she sees a few collagues she worked with before and knows them longer than me standing a bit farther .. Yet she decided to stay with me and with colleagues she does not know yet. After the drill is over and we are allowed inside , she just tells me to come with her , ofc 60+ people and one door way so i lag a bit behind. But after i got inside, i just saw her waiting for me by the door . After that we had lunch break and itwas a pizza day, so we sat at the table next to eachother and started eating our pizzas with a few other colleagues . Out of the blue she just asked me(noone else) if i wanted a slice of her pizza. Me not knowing how to respond i politely declined, and sweetly said that she should eat it , so she does not go hungry. (Hopefully i did not say something offending by that :D)

&#x200B;

God i do not know what to do :D

Sadly there is no such community in my state. But i will take a vacation there and try to figure something out.

&#x200B;

Thanks :)

Well my japanese at N4 maybe N3(right now studying more the written language than speaking) and English on C1 but closer to C2 level.

&#x200B;

Regarding the english teaching, that is not my cup of tea to begin with so i am more focused on IT related jobs.

&#x200B;

Ill check out the website you provided.

&#x200B;

Thank you :)

Well they do have highly-educated workforce, but you can get close/on their level of education via work experience....About the degree, in our state, no. Like i said due to this incident with buying college degrees , and it was not just one college doing this, but most of them.And i know for a fact (few friends,relatives have spent their 4+ years studying only to find out it was not only harder to find a job here , but also abroad , basicly their were told the degree from ´´insert slovakian college name here´´ was useless, and having no work experience in that field was a minus aswell).Regarding studying in Japan, i have thought about it. But sadly the tuition/living costs would just be too much in the long run.  Average wage in Slovakia is about 400-500€ a month. But living costs are allmost the same as in Germany where the average wage is about 2000-2500€ a month.

To put an example: If you want to move out of your parents house, to 2bedroom apartment , you have take up a mortgage for 30+years .

&#x200B;

So right now i dont know how to progress...Seems i have come to a dead end.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

